IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part IV: the pilot projects about the weeks of benefits and the benefit period:
-- Pilot Project No. 6 (reg 77.2), No. 14 (reg 77.91), No. 15 (reg 77.92), No. 21 (reg 77.992) and No. 22 (reg 77.993).
-- Regs 77.3, 77.4, 77.5 and 77.6 are repealed. Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt.
-- The text is an unofficial rendering; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Every one of these pilot projects is spent (the last window closed on September 7, 2024). Each is encoded in full, with the date of the benefit period as a plain input,
-- so that each rule answers correctly for the claimant it governed. The tables of Schedules II.2, II.7 and II.93 (maximum weeks by regional rate and hours) are piece er6's:
-- each is taken as the NUMBER the table gives. Relations (Hohfeld): a pilot project gives each claimant it includes a claim to the maximum weeks or the extension it sets
-- (the Commission bears the correlative duty); reg 77.92(3) is a duty of the Commission to publish a notice.

§ `Regulations Part IV - Pilot Projects on the weeks of benefits and the benefit period`

§§ `Reg 77.2 - Pilot Project No. 6, increased weeks of benefits`

-- src:1433 | 77.2 (1) The Commission establishes Pilot Project No. 6 for the purpose of assessing the costs and impact of increasing weeks of benefits in selected economic regions.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.2(1) (src:1433)
`reg 77.2(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 6` MEANS
    "assessing the costs and impact of increasing weeks of benefits in selected economic regions"

-- src:1435 | (a) whose benefit period is established in the period beginning on June 6, 2004 and ending on June 4, 2006; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.2(2)(a) (src:1435)
`reg 77.2(2)(a) the period in which the benefit period must be established for Pilot Project No. 6` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YMD 2004 6 6), (YMD 2006 6 4)

-- (2) Pilot Project No. 6 includes each claimant (a) whose benefit period is established in the period from June 6, 2004 to June 4, 2006; and (b) who, at the time the benefit period is established,
-- is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.1.
-- src:1434 | (2) Pilot Project No. 6 includes each claimant
-- src:1435 | (a) whose benefit period is established in the period beginning on June 6, 2004 and ending on June 4, 2006; and
-- src:1436 | (b) who, at the time the benefit period is established, is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.1.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.2(2) (src:1434-1436)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period is established` IS A DATE
      `the claimant is, at that time, ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.1` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Schedule II.1 (piece er6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.2(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6` IF
        `the day` `the day on which the benefit period is established` `falls within` `reg 77.2(2)(a) the period in which the benefit period must be established for Pilot Project No. 6`
    AND `the claimant is, at that time, ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.1`

-- (3) Despite s 12(2) of the Act, the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period established for an included claimant is determined by the table in Schedule II.2,
-- by reference to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period. NOTHING for a claimant not included: s 12(2) governs (piece ei1).
-- src:1437 | (3) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Act, the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period that is established for a claimant who is included in Pilot Project No. 6 shall be determined in accordance with the table set out in Schedule II.2 by reference to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the number of hours of insurable employment of the claimant in their qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.2(3) (src:1437)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks that the table in Schedule II.2 gives for the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: Schedule II.2 (piece er6)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.2(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` IS
    IF `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6`
    THEN JUST `the number of weeks that the table in Schedule II.2 gives for the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regs 77.3 to 77.6 - repealed`

-- Each reads only "[Repealed, SOR/2011-127, s. 1]", "[Repealed, SOR/2016-206, s. 7]" or "[Repealed, SOR/2010-214, s. 1]". A labelled stub, with no operative outcome.
-- src:1438 | 77.3 [Repealed, SOR/2011-127, s. 1]
-- src:1439 | 77.4 [Repealed, SOR/2011-127, s. 1]
-- src:1440 | 77.5 [Repealed, SOR/2016-206, s. 7]
-- src:1441 | 77.6 [Repealed, SOR/2010-214, s. 1]
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 77.3 to 77.6 (src:1438-1441)
`regs 77.3 to 77.6 are repealed and therefore not encoded` MEANS
        "77.3 [Repealed, SOR/2011-127, s. 1]"
    ... "77.4 [Repealed, SOR/2011-127, s. 1]"
    ... "77.5 [Repealed, SOR/2016-206, s. 7]"
    ... "77.6 [Repealed, SOR/2010-214, s. 1]"

§§ `Reg 77.91 - Pilot Project No. 14, extended benefit period and training incentive`

-- src:1469 | 77.91 (1) Pilot Project No. 14 is established for the purposes of assessing whether the extension of the number of weeks of benefits paid to a qualified claimant who undertakes long-term training encourages the claimant to pursue such training and improves their re-employability.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.91(1) (src:1469)
`reg 77.91(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 14` MEANS
    "assessing whether the extension of the number of weeks of benefits paid to a qualified claimant who undertakes long-term training encourages the claimant to pursue such training and improves their re-employability"

-- src:1470 | (2) Pilot Project No. 14 applies in respect of every claimant whose benefit period is established in the period beginning on January 25, 2009 and ending on May 29, 2010.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.91(2) (src:1470)
`reg 77.91(2) the period in which the benefit period must be established for Pilot Project No. 14` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 1 25), (YMD 2010 5 29)

-- (3) Pilot Project No. 14 applies to every claimant who meets the criteria: (a) at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium contributed in at least seven of the 10 years before the benefit period;
-- (b) paid less than 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before the benefit period; (c) within 20 weeks after the beginning of the benefit period, or before August 23, 2009 if the benefit period began
-- before May 31, 2009, the claimant has an active return to work action plan; and (d) the claimant is referred by the Commission, or an authority it designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act to a course
-- or program that is full-time, lasts at least 20 weeks, and begins during one of the 52 weeks following the beginning of the benefit period but not before May 31, 2009.
-- Readings taken: (c) is "within 20 weeks ... or ... before August 23, 2009 if the benefit period began before May 31, 2009", two alternatives of which the second is open only to the early benefit periods (fork F-reg77.91c);
-- the plan is "active" from the day it became active, so a plan that became active earlier counts; "the 52 weeks following the beginning" are the 52 weeks that start with the first day of the benefit period (fork F-reg77.91d).
-- src:1471 | (3) Pilot Project No. 14 applies in respect of every claimant who meets the following criteria:
-- src:1472 | (a) the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in at least seven of the 10 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period;
-- src:1473 | (b) the claimant was paid less than 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period;
-- src:1474 | (c) within 20 weeks after the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period or before August 23, 2009, if the benefit period began before May 31, 2009, the claimant has an active return to work action plan; and
-- src:1475 | (d) the claimant is referred by the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, to a course or program of instruction or training
-- src:1476 | (i) that is full-time,
-- src:1477 | (ii) that has a duration of at least 20 weeks, and
-- src:1478 | (iii) that begins during one of the 52 weeks following the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period, but not before May 31, 2009.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.91(3) (src:1471-1478)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period begins` IS A DATE
      `the years among the 10 years before the beginning of the benefit period in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of regular benefits paid to the claimant in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the claimant's return to work action plan became active, if the claimant has one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the claimant is referred by the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, to a course or program of instruction or training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the course or program is full-time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the course or program has a duration in weeks of` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the course or program begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` IF
        `the years among the 10 years before the beginning of the benefit period in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium` AT LEAST 7
    AND `the weeks of regular benefits paid to the claimant in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` LESS THAN 36
    AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the claimant's return to work action plan became active, if the claimant has one`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST plan THEN (plan AT MOST (`the last day of` (`weeks as days` 20) `days after` `the day on which the benefit period begins`)) OR (`the day on which the benefit period begins` BELOW (YMD 2009 5 31) AND plan BELOW (YMD 2009 8 23)))
    AND `the claimant is referred by the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, to a course or program of instruction or training`
    AND `the course or program is full-time`
    AND `the course or program has a duration in weeks of` AT LEAST 20
    AND `the day on which the course or program begins` AT LEAST `the day on which the benefit period begins`
    AND `the day on which the course or program begins` AT MOST (`the last day of` ((`weeks as days` 52) MINUS 1) `days after` `the day on which the benefit period begins`)
    AND `the day on which the course or program begins` AT LEAST (YMD 2009 5 31)

-- (2) and (3) together: the pilot project applies to every claimant whose benefit period is established in the period from January 25, 2009 to May 29, 2010 and who meets the criteria of (3).
-- src:1470 | (2) Pilot Project No. 14 applies in respect of every claimant whose benefit period is established in the period beginning on January 25, 2009 and ending on May 29, 2010.
-- src:1471 | (3) Pilot Project No. 14 applies in respect of every claimant who meets the following criteria:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.91(2), reg 77.91(3) (src:1470-1471)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period is established` IS A DATE
      `the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.91(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14` IF
        `the day` `the day on which the benefit period is established` `falls within` `reg 77.91(2) the period in which the benefit period must be established for Pilot Project No. 14`
    AND `the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14`

-- (6) For the application of (4) and (5), the period granted for job-search purposes is one week of benefits for every five weeks of training completed, up to a maximum of 12 consecutive weeks.
-- "For every five weeks" is read as every complete five weeks (fork F-reg77.91f). This period begins on the Sunday after the last day on which the claimant attends the course or program.
-- src:1483 | (6) For the application of subsections (4) and (5), the period granted for job-search purposes is equal to one week of benefits for every five weeks of training completed, up to a maximum of 12 consecutive weeks. This period begins on the Sunday after the last day on which the claimant attends the course or program.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.91(6) (src:1483)
GIVEN `the weeks of training the claimant has completed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` IS
    min 12 (FLOOR (`the weeks of training the claimant has completed` DIVIDED BY 5))

-- src:1483 | (6) For the application of subsections (4) and (5), the period granted for job-search purposes is equal to one week of benefits for every five weeks of training completed, up to a maximum of 12 consecutive weeks. This period begins on the Sunday after the last day on which the claimant attends the course or program.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.91(6) (src:1483)
GIVEN `the last day on which the claimant attends the course or program` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 77.91(6) the Sunday on which the period granted for job-search purposes begins` IS
    `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the last day on which the claimant attends the course or program` PLUS 7

-- (4) Despite s 10(2) and (8) of the Act, the benefit period of a claimant included in the project is extended by the duration in weeks of the course or program, including any periods of interruption, and
-- the period granted for job-search purposes, up to a maximum of 104 weeks. Reading taken (fork F-reg77.91e): the 104 weeks cap the extension; it is not a cap on the length of the benefit period as extended.
-- src:1479 | (4) Despite subsections 10(2) and (8) of the Act, the benefit period of a claimant who is included in Pilot Project No. 14 is extended by the duration, in weeks, of the course or program referred to in paragraph (3)(d) — including any periods of interruption of the course or program — and the period granted for job-search purposes, up to a maximum of 104 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.91(4) (src:1479)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duration in weeks of the course or program, including any periods of interruption` IS A NUMBER
      `the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.91(4) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` IS
    IF `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14`
    THEN min 104 (`the duration in weeks of the course or program, including any periods of interruption` PLUS `the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks`)
    ELSE 0

-- (7) If any of the conditions under which the Commission may terminate the claimant's referral under paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act exists, (5) ceases to apply on the Sunday after the last day of attendance.
-- src:1484 | (7) If any of the conditions under which the Commission may terminate the claimant’s referral under paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act exists, subsection (5) ceases to apply on the Sunday after the last day on which the claimant attends the course or program.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.91(7) (src:1484)
GIVEN `any of the conditions under which the Commission may terminate the claimant's referral under paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act exists` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 27(1.1)(b) of the Act (piece ei2)
      `the last day on which the claimant attends the course or program` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 77.91(7) the Sunday on which subsection 77.91(5) ceases to apply` IS
    IF `any of the conditions under which the Commission may terminate the claimant's referral under paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act exists`
    THEN JUST (`reg 77.91(6) the Sunday on which the period granted for job-search purposes begins` `the last day on which the claimant attends the course or program`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to an included claimant is the number determined by s 12(2), (3) or (6) of the Act added to, if applicable, the number of weeks that fall within the
-- benefit period established under (4) (a) during which the claimant is attending the course or program or is searching for a job during the period granted for that purpose; and (b) for which no benefits are payable under s 12(1).
-- Once (7) has ended the effect of (5), the number is the one the Act gives.
-- src:1480 | (5) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to a claimant who is included in Pilot Project No. 14 is that which is determined by any of subsections 12(2), (3) or (6) of the Act added to, if applicable, the number of weeks that fall within the benefit period established under subsection (4)
-- src:1481 | (a) during which the claimant is attending the course or program referred to in paragraph (3)(d) or is searching for a job during the period granted for that purpose; and
-- src:1482 | (b) for which no benefits are payable under subsection 12(1) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.91(5) (src:1480-1482)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum number of weeks determined by subsection 12(2), (3) or (6) of the Act` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: s 12(2), (3), (6) of the Act (piece ei1)
      `the weeks within the benefit period established under subsection 77.91(4) during which the claimant is attending the course or program or is searching for a job during the period granted for that purpose, and for which no benefits are payable under subsection 12(1) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `subsection 77.91(5) has ceased to apply under subsection 77.91(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.91(5) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` IS
    IF     `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14`
       AND (NOT `subsection 77.91(5) has ceased to apply under subsection 77.91(7)`)
    THEN `the maximum number of weeks determined by subsection 12(2), (3) or (6) of the Act` PLUS `the weeks within the benefit period established under subsection 77.91(4) during which the claimant is attending the course or program or is searching for a job during the period granted for that purpose, and for which no benefits are payable under subsection 12(1) of the Act`
    ELSE `the maximum number of weeks determined by subsection 12(2), (3) or (6) of the Act`

§§ `Reg 77.92 - Pilot Project No. 15, extended benefits`

-- src:1487 | 77.92 (1) Pilot Project No. 15 is established for the purpose of assessing the costs and impact of extending the number of weeks of benefits in selected economic regions.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.92(1) (src:1487)
`reg 77.92(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 15` MEANS
    "assessing the costs and impact of extending the number of weeks of benefits in selected economic regions"

-- The second Saturday after a day: the first Saturday strictly after it, and seven days more. (Saturday is the day whose count modulo 7 is 6; Sunday is the one whose count modulo 7 is 0, as in the keel.)
-- src:1491 | (i) if the regional rate of unemployment, as determined in accordance with subsection 17(1), is less than 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods, beginning after October 9, 2010, in the region in respect of which the benefit period was established, on the second Saturday after the first day of the 12th period, or
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.92(2)(b)(i) (src:1491)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `er5 reg 77.92 the second Saturday after the day` IS
    d PLUS ((IF (Day d MODULO 7) EQUALS 6 THEN 7 ELSE 6 MINUS (Day d MODULO 7)) PLUS 7)

-- (2)(b) The benefit period is established in the period that begins on September 12, 2010 and ends (i) if the regional rate of unemployment, as determined in accordance with s 17(1), is less than 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods,
-- beginning after October 9, 2010, in the region in respect of which the benefit period was established, on the second Saturday after the first day of the 12th period, or (ii) in any other case, on September 15, 2012.
-- Taken literally: (i) is not cut off by the date of (ii).
-- src:1490 | (b) whose benefit period is established in the period beginning on September 12, 2010 and ending
-- src:1491 | (i) if the regional rate of unemployment, as determined in accordance with subsection 17(1), is less than 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods, beginning after October 9, 2010, in the region in respect of which the benefit period was established, on the second Saturday after the first day of the 12th period, or
-- src:1492 | (ii) in any other case, on September 15, 2012.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.92(2)(b) (src:1490-1492)
GIVEN `the regional rate of unemployment, as determined in accordance with subsection 17(1), is less than 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods, beginning after October 9, 2010, in the region in respect of which the benefit period was established` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: reg 17(1) (piece er1)
      `the first day of the 12th of those periods` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 77.92(2)(b) the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` IS
    IF `the regional rate of unemployment, as determined in accordance with subsection 17(1), is less than 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods, beginning after October 9, 2010, in the region in respect of which the benefit period was established`
    THEN `er5 reg 77.92 the second Saturday after the day` `the first day of the 12th of those periods`
    ELSE YMD 2012 9 15

-- (2) applies to every claimant (a) who, at the time their benefit period is established, is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.6; and
-- (b) whose benefit period is established in the period that begins on September 12, 2010 and ends on the day (2)(b) gives.
-- src:1488 | (2) Pilot Project No. 15 applies in respect of every claimant
-- src:1489 | (a) who, at the time that their benefit period is established, is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.6; and
-- src:1490 | (b) whose benefit period is established in the period beginning on September 12, 2010 and ending
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.92(2) (src:1488-1490)
GIVEN `the claimant is, at the time their benefit period is established, ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.6` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Schedule II.6 (piece er6)
      `the day on which the benefit period is established` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` IF
        `the claimant is, at the time their benefit period is established, ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.6`
    AND `the day on which the benefit period is established` AT LEAST (YMD 2010 9 12)
    AND `the day on which the benefit period is established` AT MOST `the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15`

-- (3) If the condition referred to in subparagraph (2)(b)(i) is satisfied, the Commission must, as soon as possible, publish a notice in the Canada Gazette that specifies the day on which the establishment of benefit periods ends
-- in the region in question, and must also publish the notice on its website. No number of days is given for "as soon as possible".
-- src:1493 | (3) If the condition referred to in subparagraph (2)(b)(i) is satisfied, the Commission must, as soon as possible, publish a notice in the Canada Gazette that specifies the day on which the establishment of benefit periods ends, in the region in question, under Pilot Project No. 15. The Commission must also publish the notice on its website.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.92(3) (src:1493)
GIVEN `the condition referred to in subparagraph 77.92(2)(b)(i) is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.92(3) the Commission must publish a notice in the Canada Gazette and on its website` IF
    `the condition referred to in subparagraph 77.92(2)(b)(i) is satisfied`

-- (4) Despite s 12(2) of the Act, the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period established for an included claimant is determined by the table in Schedule II.7, by reference to the regional rate of unemployment that
-- applies to the claimant and the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period.
-- src:1494 | (4) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Act, the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period that is established for a claimant who is included in Pilot Project No. 15 shall be determined in accordance with the table set out in Schedule II.7 by reference to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the number of hours of insurable employment of the claimant in their qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.92(4) (src:1494)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks that the table in Schedule II.7 gives for the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: Schedule II.7 (piece er6)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.92(4) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` IS
    IF `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15`
    THEN JUST `the number of weeks that the table in Schedule II.7 gives for the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Reg 77.992 - Pilot Project No. 21, increased weeks of benefits for seasonal workers`

-- src:1578 | 77.992 (1) Pilot Project No. 21 is established for the purpose of testing the effectiveness of a mechanism that targets persons who meet the criteria set out in subsection (2) and testing the outcomes of increasing the number of weeks of benefits paid to the targeted population.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.992(1) (src:1578)
`reg 77.992(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 21` MEANS
    "testing the effectiveness of a mechanism that targets persons who meet the criteria set out in subsection (2) and testing the outcomes of increasing the number of weeks of benefits paid to the targeted population"

-- (4) For the purposes of (2)(d), a benefit period in a previous year is considered to have begun around the same time of year if it began during the period that begins eight weeks before and ends eight weeks after the week that is
-- (a) 52, (b) 104, (c) 156, (d) 208 or (e) 260 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in (2)(a). Weeks run Sunday to Saturday, so the period runs from the first day of the eighth week before
-- to the last day of the eighth week after (fork F-reg77.992). The week that is n weeks before the first week begins n times seven days before the Sunday that begins that first week.
-- src:1585 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(d), a benefit period in a previous year is considered to have begun around the same time of year if it began during the period that begins eight weeks before and ends eight weeks after the week that is
-- src:1586 | (a) 52 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a);
-- src:1587 | (b) 104 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a);
-- src:1588 | (c) 156 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a);
-- src:1589 | (d) 208 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a); or
-- src:1590 | (e) 260 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph (2)(a).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.992(4) (src:1585-1590)
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the earlier benefit period began` IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks before that first week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `er5 reg 77.992 the earlier benefit period began within eight weeks before or after the week that is a number of weeks before the first week` IF
        Day `the day on which the earlier benefit period began`
            AT LEAST ((Day `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` MINUS `weeks as days` `the number of weeks before that first week`) MINUS (`weeks as days` 8))
    AND Day `the day on which the earlier benefit period began`
            AT MOST (((Day `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` MINUS `weeks as days` `the number of weeks before that first week`) PLUS (`weeks as days` 8)) PLUS 6)

-- src:1585 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(d), a benefit period in a previous year is considered to have begun around the same time of year if it began during the period that begins eight weeks before and ends eight weeks after the week that is
