    OR  `er5 reg 77.992 the earlier benefit period began within eight weeks before or after the week that is a number of weeks before the first week` `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` `the day on which the earlier benefit period began` 104
    OR  `er5 reg 77.992 the earlier benefit period began within eight weeks before or after the week that is a number of weeks before the first week` `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` `the day on which the earlier benefit period began` 156
    OR  `er5 reg 77.992 the earlier benefit period began within eight weeks before or after the week that is a number of weeks before the first week` `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` `the day on which the earlier benefit period began` 208
    OR  `er5 reg 77.992 the earlier benefit period began within eight weeks before or after the week that is a number of weeks before the first week` `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` `the day on which the earlier benefit period began` 260

-- (3) For the purposes of (2)(c), a claimant's benefit period established before the beginning of the 260-week period is considered to have been established within the 260-week period if the claimant received
-- a notification of payment or non-payment with respect to any week that falls within that 260-week period. The 260 weeks are the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period of (2)(a).
-- src:1584 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(c), a claimant’s benefit period established before the beginning of the 260-week period is considered to have been established within the 260-week period if the claimant received a notification of payment or non-payment with respect to any week that falls within that 260-week period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.992(3) (src:1584)
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the earlier benefit period was established` IS A DATE
      `the claimant received a notification of payment or non-payment with respect to a week that falls within the 260-week period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.992(3) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260-week period` IF
        (Day `the day on which the earlier benefit period was established`) AT MOST (Day `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)`)
    AND (   (Day `the day on which the earlier benefit period was established`) AT LEAST ((Day `the Sunday that begins the first week of the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)`) MINUS (`weeks as days` 260))
         OR `the claimant received a notification of payment or non-payment with respect to a week that falls within the 260-week period`)

-- (2)(c) and (d): at least three benefit periods established in the 260 weeks during which regular benefits were paid or payable; and at least two of those began around the same time of year as the benefit period of (2)(a).
-- The counts are the claimant's, made with (3) and (4).
-- src:1582 | (c) in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period referred to in paragraph (a), at least three benefit periods had been established during which regular benefits were paid or payable; and
-- src:1583 | (d) at least two of the benefit periods referred to in paragraph (c) had begun around the same time of year as the benefit period referred to in paragraph (a) began.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.992(2)(c), reg 77.992(2)(d) (src:1582-1583)
GIVEN `the number of benefit periods established in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period during which regular benefits were paid or payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.992(2)(c) at least three benefit periods had been established` IF
    `the number of benefit periods established in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period during which regular benefits were paid or payable` AT LEAST 3

-- src:1583 | (d) at least two of the benefit periods referred to in paragraph (c) had begun around the same time of year as the benefit period referred to in paragraph (a) began.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.992(2)(d) (src:1583)
GIVEN `the number of those benefit periods that had begun around the same time of year as the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.992(2)(d) at least two of those benefit periods had begun around the same time of year` IF
    `the number of those benefit periods that had begun around the same time of year as the benefit period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` AT LEAST 2

-- (2) Pilot Project No. 21 applies to every claimant who meets the criteria: (a) the date on which a benefit period is established falls within the period from August 5, 2018 to September 25, 2021;
-- (b) at the time the benefit period is established, the claimant is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.92; (c); and (d).
-- src:1579 | (2) Pilot Project No. 21 applies to every claimant who meets the following criteria:
-- src:1580 | (a) the date on which a benefit period is established falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2018 and ending on September 25, 2021;
-- src:1581 | (b) at the time that the benefit period is established, the claimant is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.92;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.992(2) (src:1579-1581)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period is established` IS A DATE
      `the claimant is, at that time, ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.92` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Schedule II.92 (piece er6)
      `at least three benefit periods had been established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at least two of those benefit periods had begun around the same time of year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` IF
        `the day on which the benefit period is established` AT LEAST (YMD 2018 8 5)
    AND `the day on which the benefit period is established` AT MOST (YMD 2021 9 25)
    AND `the claimant is, at that time, ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.92`
    AND `at least three benefit periods had been established`
    AND `at least two of those benefit periods had begun around the same time of year`

-- (5) Despite s 12(2) of the Act, the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period established for an included claimant is determined by the table in Schedule II.93.
-- src:1591 | (5) Despite subsection 12(2) of the Act, the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period that is established for a claimant who is included in Pilot Project No. 21 shall be determined in accordance with the table set out in Schedule II.93 by reference to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the number of hours of insurable employment of the claimant in their qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.992(5) (src:1591)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks that the table in Schedule II.93 gives for the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: Schedule II.93 (piece er6)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.992(5) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` IS
    IF `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21`
    THEN JUST `the number of weeks that the table in Schedule II.93 gives for the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Reg 77.993 - Pilot Project No. 22, additional weeks for seasonal workers`

-- src:1594 | 77.993 (1) Pilot Project No. 22 is established for the purpose of testing whether certain claimants who meet the conditions set out in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act require more additional weeks of benefits as a result of low unemployment rates.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.993(1) (src:1594)
`reg 77.993(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 22` MEANS
    "testing whether certain claimants who meet the conditions set out in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act require more additional weeks of benefits as a result of low unemployment rates"

-- (3) For the purposes of the project, the reference to "Schedule V" in the portion of s 12(2.3) before paragraph (a) is read as a reference to "Schedule II.94 of the Employment Insurance Regulations".
-- src:1596 | (3) For the purposes of Pilot Project No. 22, the reference to “Schedule V” in the portion of subsection 12(2.3) of the Act before paragraph (a) shall be read as a reference to “Schedule II.94 of the Employment Insurance Regulations”.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.993(3) (src:1596)
`reg 77.993(3) the schedule that is read in place of Schedule V in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act` MEANS
    "Schedule II.94 of the Employment Insurance Regulations"

-- (2) Pilot Project No. 22 applies to every claimant whose benefit period is established in the period from September 10, 2023 to September 7, 2024 and who meets the conditions set out in s 12(2.3) of the Act
-- (read with Schedule II.94 for Schedule V, by (3)). Whether the conditions are met is decided by the Act (piece ei1) and Schedule II.94 (piece er6): a BOOLEAN input.
-- src:1595 | (2) Pilot Project No. 22 applies to every claimant whose benefit period is established in the period beginning on September 10, 2023 and ending on September 7, 2024 and who meets the conditions set out in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.993(2) (src:1595)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period is established` IS A DATE
      `the claimant meets the conditions set out in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act, read with Schedule II.94 in place of Schedule V` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 12(2.3) of the Act (piece ei1) and Schedule II.94 (piece er6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.993(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 22` IF
        `the day on which the benefit period is established` AT LEAST (YMD 2023 9 10)
    AND `the day on which the benefit period is established` AT MOST (YMD 2024 9 7)
    AND `the claimant meets the conditions set out in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act, read with Schedule II.94 in place of Schedule V`
